virglrenderer: flush a GL context before switching away from it (macOS)

What: vrend_sync_make_current(), vrend's switch to another GL context with a
fence the next context waits for, calls glFlush() after glFenceSync() and
before the switch. Two callers cross contexts on the Mac, both there and
back: the re-stride of a Vulkan window without a copy (Hyprland's context ->
the blitter's -> Hyprland's, virgl-vulkan-windows-iosurface.patch) and the GL
fallback of vrend_renderer_blit_int (the guest's context -> the blitter's ->
the guest's).
Why: a glWaitSync in another context waits only for a fence that was flushed
(ARB_sync). eglMakeCurrent and glXMakeCurrent flush the context they leave,
and upstream relies on that; QEMU's Cocoa make_current is a plain
CGLSetCurrentContext, which does not, and Apple's glWaitSync on an unflushed
fence does not wait. So the next context's draw ran before the other
context's commands were even sent. Hyprland showed a Vulkan window with that
buffer's previous frame in the first composite after every new frame (Zed's
caret one character back for a frame, #499), a continuous FIFO window was one
swapchain cycle late, and a mailbox window tore. With this patch the ordering
note in vrend_resource_heap_refresh (virgl-vulkan-windows-iosurface.patch)
holds.
Upstream: could go upstream (on EGL and GLX the extra flush finds nothing to
send).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-vulkan-window-handover.c (build time, on the GPU: the
real vrend_blitter_restride and vrend_sync_make_current with shared CGL
contexts, blitter -> guest and guest -> blitter; both fail without this
patch); VM rows in the track notes vk-flicker.md.

--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -2969,6 +2969,11 @@
 
 void vrend_sync_make_current(virgl_gl_context gl_cxt) {
    GLsync sync = glFenceSync(GL_SYNC_GPU_COMMANDS_COMPLETE, 0);
+   /* The other context's glWaitSync only waits for a fence that was flushed
+    * (ARB_sync). eglMakeCurrent and glXMakeCurrent flush the context they
+    * leave; macOS's CGLSetCurrentContext does not, so the other context ran
+    * before this one's commands were even sent. */
+   glFlush();
    vrend_clicbs->make_current(gl_cxt);
    glWaitSync(sync, 0, GL_TIMEOUT_IGNORED);
    glDeleteSync(sync);
